course: dictionary
lesson: 5352
title: What a kilowatt measures
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A kilowatt, written kW, is a unit of power. Power tells you how fast a machine uses or makes energy. One kilowatt is 1,000 watts, so a 2-kilowatt heater uses 2,000 watts.
explain: Electricity bills count energy in kilowatt-hours, written kWh. One kilowatt-hour is 1 kilowatt used for 1 hour. If a 2 kW heater runs for 1 hour, it uses 2 kWh.
explain: Read this: «The electricity meter counts how much the home uses in kilowatt-hours, and a smart meter sends the reading automatically.» Then read «a kettle uses more power than a whole room of LED lights.» A kettle is a machine that uses a lot of power quickly, so it is measured in kilowatts. Each LED light uses much less.
fact: A kilowatt is 1,000 watts, so 1 kW = 1,000 W.
fact: A kilowatt measures power, which is how fast energy is used or made.
fact: A kilowatt-hour (kWh) is the energy used by 1 kilowatt running for 1 hour.
fact: Kettles, heaters and car engines are rated in kilowatts (kW).
fact: To change watts to kilowatts, divide by 1,000: 2,500 W is 2.5 kW.
exercise: What is 1 kilowatt equal to? | * 1,000 watts | 10 watts | 100 watts | 1,000,000 watts
exercise: «The electricity meter counts how much the home uses in kilowatt-hours.» What unit does the meter count in? | Kilometres | Degrees | Litres | * Kilowatt-hours
exercise: A 2-kilowatt heater is on for 3 hours. How many kilowatt-hours does it use? | 23 kWh | 2 kWh | * 6 kWh | 5 kWh
test: A kettle uses 1,500 watts. How many kilowatts is that? | 15 kW | 150 kW | 0.015 kW | * 1.5 kW
test: «A kettle uses more power than a whole room of LED lights.» Which uses more power? | LED lights | Neither uses power | They use the same power | * The kettle
exam: Which unit measures how fast an electrical machine uses energy? | Kilometre | Kilolitre | Kilogram | * Kilowatt
